<title>USA: Clinton does not want rise in deficit with Japan.</title>
<headline>Clinton does not want rise in deficit with Japan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton said Friday that the United States does not want a resurgence in its trade deficit with Japan.</p>
<p>He made the remarks to reporters at the start of a meeting with Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto.</p>
<p>Asked if he will bring up the issue of the trade deficit with Japan, Clinton said the issue will be discussed with the prime minister.</p>
<p>Japan's trade surplus with the United States rose 11.2 percent to $3.04 billion in March, the sixth consecutive month in which it had risen year on year.</p>
</text>
